(49, 5, 2, 16080, 19280, 'speaker_1', 'climate events that are destabilizing and impactful', NULL),
(50, 5, 3, 20320, 47680, 'speaker_1', 'the rise of darker energies that might want to whether they want it to look like a war or whether they want it to look like people being more divided amongst themselves i think that is the shadow side of what we\'re in as a world and i think for those of us who remember say the nineties or the eighties or the you know even the early or you know the two oh oh ohs i think it\'s quite', NULL),
(51, 5, 4, 49440, 98120, 'speaker_1', 'impactful to walk through that as an energy field and i think about the people i meet who in their seventies and eighties who are walking through it and i\'m like wow you have seen some change because the climate is so different and there is this i think very intense energy in the world i felt it when i was touring and i was going to all these different cities you know i would just walk and pay attention and see how people were looking feeling being and of course cities are always a a skewed example because if you go to smaller towns or local more community based places you can feel softer energy but cities are a good example of of seeing how are people doing with all of this and for me there is the the overarching thing i could feel was how exhausting these times are for everyone', NULL),
(52, 5, 5, 99720, 140000, 'speaker_1', 'very tiring times to go through it doesn\'t mean that\'s all it is and it doesn\'t mean you can\'t be having the best time of your life right now in some areas of your life there might be certain things in your life right now that are the most joyous the most impactful the most than than they\'ve ever been but just the temperature temperature of the world literally there is this kind of overwhelm and yet within it and this is the interesting part spiritual energy is ratcheting up in people\'s lives whether people are coming to it through visitations from angels or dead loved ones or who\'ve passed over', NULL),
(53, 5, 6, 141040, 181640, 'speaker_1', 'more people are having more mystical experiences in the world with the land people reporting et experiences all of that is very strong right now and that\'s one of the things my guide\'s the z\'s had said they said you\'re gonna go through times on earth that will in a way dismantle your old world and in tandem with that you will see a massive rise in consciousness and at the time they said that maybe fifteen years ago i remember thinking oh i had an idea of what that would look like but what i\'m seeing is it\'s very varied and it\'s very personal recently i was talking to someone who was upset about', NULL),
(54, 5, 7, 182920, 231240, 'speaker_1', 'someone that they knew in the spiritual field who was known who had now gone to jesus in christ consciousness and religion which we\'re seeing a lot and vice versa i\'ve also seen people walk away from religion during this time or you know shift into spirituality and the message my guides have always given me is it doesn\'t really matter how you are finding faith for yourself how your faith makes you behave toward others that\'s very interesting so you know i\'ve always said that i personally have never grown up in religion but i support any religion that helps people love each other more and become more of who they\'re here to be and live a more spirit filled life that\'s harmonic i don\'t support religion\'s disguise', NULL),
(55, 5, 8, 232280, 250960, 'speaker_1', 'as war machines you know that a lot of religion will try and annihilate certain groups or certain people and and say it\'s in the name of god and it\'s like well who\'s god because there\'s a god on the other side of the world that the group you\'re trying to kill are are also believing in so i i think the reason i share that is just', NULL),
(56, 5, 9, 252000, 293280, 'speaker_1', 'it\'s one of the themes i put in this month\'s energy update there is this weird almost breakdown around what spirituality religion faith is i\'m a big believer in christ consciousness and jesus i can i can connect to that energy and still connect to other energies i don\'t believe i have to be ring fenced into seeing that a certain way so you know that\'s what i was just saying to my friend i said yeah there are those who do that and they point the finger back at where they were and try and destroy it and there are those who go oh i\'ve grown into this and that\'s okay if that\'s how they\'re now experiencing their faith but i think the reason faith is becoming more important for people is in times of turmoil and trouble', NULL),
(57, 5, 10, 294480, 308680, 'speaker_1', 'people start to go within to look for something that can support them especially when things outside seem less stable or less predictable or less holding of you than ever before', NULL),
(58, 5, 11, 310760, 322920, 'speaker_2', 'yeah that uncertainty and that less holding is can totally fill that in the air it\'s but what i\'m hearing and sorry not but and what i\'m hearing is this there\'s a dismantling almost for a remantling', NULL),
(59, 5, 12, 324200, 342920, 'speaker_2', 'to happen at this time one of the things that stayed with me somewhere along in your energy updates is you said you\'d rather be stuck in a lift with someone kind and openhearted than someone spiritually learned who isn\'t kind and openhearted', NULL),
(60, 5, 13, 342920, 343320, 'speaker_1', 'yes', NULL),
(61, 5, 14, 343960, 369840, 'speaker_2', 'there\'s something about that that really stayed with me because it makes me wonder sometimes there\'s so many things about that but one of them that\'s you know a predisposition as well because i i\'ve met some people that have just arrived on the planet kind you know they never studied any of the work that you studied they\'ve never studied they\'ve never listened to one of your updates they\'ve never listened to my podcast they\'re just kind souls you know i\'ve got family members like this', NULL),
(62, 5, 15, 371200, 386320, 'speaker_2', 'yeah i mean what what is that do you think some of those people just they get it from another life or they just come in a little bit more whole but then there\'s also this whole theme you know it it\'s a big ode to integration as well in many ways as well i mean i just wanted to yeah you mentioned that so it just came up for me', NULL),
(63, 5, 16, 386320, 396960, 'speaker_1', 'i love that you bring this up and my perspective on this is that we are a culture who has wrongly been taught to worship the construct rather than the effect the construct gives us', NULL),
(64, 5, 17, 398000, 401520, 'speaker_1', 'so you can be a very kind atheist', NULL),
(65, 5, 18, 403280, 409840, 'speaker_1', 'being an atheist doesn\'t make you less kind equally being spiritually learned doesn\'t make you more kind', NULL),
(66, 5, 19, 410880, 444920, 'speaker_1', 'and i think in the same way that in in you know that you can see religious groups fight each other i\'ve seen it in the spiritual field as well you meet people who want to you know feel superior to someone who isn\'t intuitive or they think because they\'ve done thirty ayahuasca trips that they are now far more enlightened than their grandmother who they see as closed minded but actually their grandmother might be the one going around the town checking everyone\'s okay whereas they\'re like off on their own you know their own', NULL),
(67, 5, 20, 445960, 481680, 'speaker_1', 'journey and there\'s nothing wrong with either journey the problem is when we start pointing the finger at other people\'s journey and so i think there can be as much judgment in the spiritual community as there is in any community because you know humans are in the spiritual community and i think for a long time certainly when i was coming up even i had this belief a bit in in my late teens and early twenties when i was first reading books and going i was taking myself off to self growth workshops and spiritual workshops i think i thought that spirituality was going to make everything better', NULL),
(68, 5, 21, 482960, 509040, 'speaker_1', 'and that\'s why we were doing it it\'s like it\'s gonna make everything better and we\'re gonna be enlightened and there\'s gonna be no distress and actually that\'s not earth school there are certainly aspects of spirituality and connection to a faith that can that can root you and that can help you be a better person in the world and help you experience the world in a better way but we\'re here on an evolutionary path and i think too often the construct', NULL),
(69, 5, 22, 510160, 515840, 'speaker_1', 'has been proclaimed as the thing so it\'s like catholicism is the way or', NULL),
(70, 5, 23, 517120, 522000, 'speaker_1', 'angel cards are the way or you know whatever it is', NULL),
(71, 5, 24, 523120, 547960, 'speaker_1', 'raw food juicing is the way and and the truth is perhaps the people who proclaim that for them maybe it was or they\'ve decided that they they\'re just limited in sight they\'re not seeing anyone else in the world because they\'re so obsessed with their own raw juice lifestyle and they think everyone else is wrong that they\'ve put two and two together and come up with five so it\'s i for me', NULL),
(72, 5, 25, 550040, 554840, 'speaker_1', 'the reason i say that and i\'ve said that a few times from stages too is', NULL),
(73, 5, 26, 556920, 566760, 'speaker_1', 'was very aware when i first started doing this work i went from being a student of self growth and spirituality to sometimes being a teacher in that arena in two oh oh four', NULL),
(74, 5, 27, 568040, 570680, 'speaker_1', 'and i\'m still a student i always will be', NULL),
(75, 5, 28, 572440, 578280, 'speaker_1', 'but what i noticed was this tendency to give our power away to teachers to teachings to', NULL),
(76, 5, 29, 579320, 640080, 'speaker_1', 'books to philosophies and as i met more of the humans behind some of those things i was like oh we\'re all still human and equally if people project onto me oh it must be amazing you know you\'ve you\'ve got the the z\'s everything must just be perfect and i\'m like no no i\'m i\'m human and i\'m going through all my own evolution too yeah it\'s not the kind of life i had thirty years ago that\'s for sure because my vantage point my perspective is so different now but it doesn\'t mean those parts of me that were five years old and ten years old have been annihilated they\'re also growing through me and so i think that\'s where my statement came from because i\'d met such brilliant atheists that i would love to be around and equally i\'d met some spiritual people who were using their spirituality as superiority or as a mask and again it\'s okay they can they can do what they want they can be who they want we have to decide', NULL),
(77, 5, 30, 641760, 703880, 'speaker_1', 'who we are how we want to interact and what\'s important to us that\'s and that goes back to the empath narcissist dynamic i think think when you come out of one of those relationships you\'re often in grief in horror in shock you can\'t quite believe that someone could have behaved that way and then you know once you get through the more victim aspects of the consciousness and i\'m not making light of that because some people go through horror with narcissists so i\'m not wanting to make light of being a victim to a narcissist in your life but you do have to get to a point where you you recognize ah where were my blind spots how did i walk into that how do i change myself so that i don\'t experience that again because that was the lesson i was being shown that was the learning from this i have to take a learning from this and use it to reclaim myself rather than live in the ashes of feeling annihilated by a relationship or an authority figure', NULL),
(78, 5, 31, 703880, 713200, 'speaker_2', 'hey there inspired evolutionary if you absolutely love this well then here\'s a full conversation with this guest on the inspired evolution podcast check it out now', NULL);
INSERT INTO `summaries` (`id`, `recording_id`, `text`, `created_at`, `action_items`, `key_points`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(3, 4, 'In the discussion, speaker 1 and speaker 2 explore the impact of different evening practices on mental and emotional health. Speaker 1 highlights the benefits of practicing gratitude before sleep, suggesting that dedicating ten minutes to gratitude can significantly enhance the immune system. In contrast, scrolling through social media, like Instagram, is described as a detrimental activity that limits independent thoughts and promotes external stimuli that can clutter the mind. Speaker 2 elaborates on the importance of self-reflection and emotional programming, emphasizing how consciously cultivating gratitude can lead to a significant shift in one\'s emotional state and overall well-being. The conversation emphasizes the value of using the evening and morning as key times for transitioning between states of consciousness, allowing for better self-awareness and personal growth. Both speakers agree that committing to gratitude and self-reflection consistently can result in profound changes in perspective and interactions with others, leading to positive life changes and an enhanced sense of personal agency.', '2026-08-14 12:27:06', '[{\"text\": \"Practice gratitude for ten minutes before bed for four days to improve immunity.\", \"endMs\": 20000, \"startMs\": 9000}, {\"text\": \"Consider the impact of spending time on Instagram versus practicing gratitude before bed.\", \"endMs\": 38000, \"startMs\": 28000}, {\"text\": \"Spend time in nature for three days to clear your mind and improve your thinking.\", \"endMs\": 91000, \"startMs\": 51000}, {\"text\": \"Engage in emotional training by feeling gratitude for future positive outcomes.\", \"endMs\": 176200, \"startMs\": 135100}, {\"text\": \"Reflect on your day to identify moments of frustration and improve your response to future situations.\", \"endMs\": 267900, \"startMs\": 177500}, {\"text\": \"Write down important things and changes you want to make before going to bed.\", \"endMs\": 320800, \"startMs\": 269900}, {\"text\": \"Invest time in personal growth before sleeping instead of using devices or watching TV.\", \"endMs\": 360200, \"startMs\": 320800}]', NULL, NULL),
(4, 5, 'In the current era, characterized by global unrest, geopolitical instability, and climate crises, the speaker reflects on the overwhelming energy present in society. They note how this heavy atmosphere affects people\'s emotional states, leading to fatigue, yet also coincide with a surge in spiritual experiences and consciousness. Many are turning inward to find faith, shifting through various forms of spirituality and religion, often leading to personal journeys that embrace a broader understanding of love and kindness over rigid belief systems. The discussion emphasizes that compassion can exist irrespective of formal religious affiliation, highlighting how certain individuals naturally embody kindness. The speaker critiques the tendency to idolize spiritual constructs or teachings, arguing that overidentifying with any particular belief or system can foster judgment and separation. They advocate for a personal evolution that draws on experiences and lessons rather than succumbing to victimhood, emphasizing the importance of agency in shaping one\'s spiritual path and responses to relationship dynamics.', '2026-08-14 13:38:36', '[]', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `hooks` (`id`, `recording_id`, `title`, `hook`, `reason`, `start_ms`, `end_ms`, `score`, `created_at`, `start_segment_id`, `end_segment_id`, `hook_type`, `context_text`, `quality_score`, `standalone_score`, `curiosity_score`, `emotional_score`, `specificity_score`, `shareability_score`, `novelty_score`, `status`, `embedding_status`, `clip_start_ms`, `clip_end_ms`, `provider`, `model`, `prompt_version`, `deleted_at`, `controversy_score`, `headline_score`) VALUES
(11, 4, 'Gratitude vs. Instagram: The Shocking Truth', 'Some people can\'t think for themselves because they\'re having something think for them.', 'It highlights a critical issue with social media engagement that many can relate to.', 40344, 52024, 0.8471544715447153, '2026-08-14 12:27:15', 36, 36, 'controversy', 'some people can\'t think for themselves because they\'re having something think for them right those images and the stimulation is causing them to really expose their brain to information', 0.9, 0.8, 0.9, 0.6, 0.8, 0.9, 0.8, 'selected', 'completed', 35640, 55320, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.9, 0.9),
(12, 4, 'Transform Your Nightly Routine', 'What if I practice gratitude before bed for ten minutes?', 'This presents a simple yet impactful change that can lead to significant health improvements.', 30504, 52024, 0.7829268292682925, '2026-08-14 12:27:15', 35, 36, 'surprise', 'what\'s if i grad if i practice gratitude before bed for ten minutes versus i use my instagram for ten minutes what\'s gonna be the difference some people can\'t think for themselves because they\'re having something think for them right those images and the stimulation is causing them to really expose their brain to information', 0.8, 0.9, 0.8, 0.7, 0.9, 0.8, 0.7, 'selected', 'completed', 25800, 55320, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.5, 0.8),
(13, 4, 'How Gratitude Changes Your Life', 'I promise you, a person who does that after a period of time is gonna feel very differently.', 'This assures the audience of a positive transformation, making it relatable.', 136824, 177864, 0.7471544715447154, '2026-08-14 12:27:15', 40, 40, 'success', 'and if i\'m having a problem with a chronic health condition or you know a immune mediated condition this would be loving to me so i\'m gonna go for ten or fifteen minutes just feeling gratitude or thinking about all the things i\'m grateful for and then i\'m gonna think about all the things that i\'ll be grateful for when they happen i\'m just gonna let myself go just i\'m just gonna play i\'m just let myself go i promise you though person who does that after a period of time is gonna feel very differently than when they spend ten minutes watching instagram right not not not that i have an opinion on it i just know that it\'s it\'s very seductive and and it could it could cause people to become very dependent on it', 0.9, 0.8, 0.7, 0.6, 0.8, 0.9, 0.6, 'selected', 'completed', 132120, 181160, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.3, 0.8),
(14, 4, 'Discovering Your Creative Power', 'Somehow it\'s kind of coming to them; that\'s all you need to believe that you\'re the creator of your life.', 'It emphasizes empowerment and creativity, encouraging self-belief.', 323744, 368424, 0.7349593495934957, '2026-08-14 12:27:15', 43, 45, 'emotion', 'somehow are coming to them it\'s not like they\'re going and having to get it like somehow it\'s kinda coming to them that\'s all you need that\'s all you need to believe that you\'re the creator of your life right and and why is that important because you\'re gonna wanna do it again you\'re gonna be like and that\'s why our community does the work because they don\'t want the magic to end they don\'t wanna jinx it they\'re like it\'s too good i\'m gonna i\'m not gonna miss my meditation because too many wonderful things are happening in my life that those synchronicities those opportunities opportunities are telling you you are in fact the creator of your life that\'s the that\'s the side effect thank you so much eclip enterprise eclipse channel subscribe', 0.8, 0.7, 0.8, 0.9, 0.6, 1, 0.6, 'selected', 'completed', 319040, 367293, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.3, 0.8),
(15, 4, 'The Secret Power of Nature', 'When you go to bed at night your serotonin levels change to melatonin.', 'This reveals the profound impact of sleep cycles on mental and emotional health.', 93344, 135784, 0.6999999999999998, '2026-08-14 12:27:15', 38, 39, 'lesson', 'a person who\'s understands that when they go to bed at night their serotonin levels change to melatonin and when you\'re in serotonin you\'re in beta when you\'re in melatonin you start dropping into alpha theta and delta and that\'s when the door opens so what do you wanna drop in there do you wanna do something you wanna drop anything in there that\'s gonna cause you to be more limited or distract you or you know you know cause you to you to think and feel later on the next day a certain way or do you say by volition i\'m gonna teach my body emotionally what my future feels like i\'m gonna keep bringing up this feeling of gratitude because i know that gratitude strengthens my immune system by fifty', 0.8, 0.7, 0.8, 0.5, 0.7, 0.7, 0.7, 'selected', 'completed', 88640, 139080, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.4, 0.8),
(16, 4, 'Rewire Your Brain Before Sleeping', 'What do you want to drop in there?', 'This poses a thought-provoking question about mindset before sleep.', 98224, 135784, 0.697560975609756, '2026-08-14 12:27:15', 39, 39, 'advice', 'their serotonin levels change to melatonin and when you\'re in serotonin you\'re in beta when you\'re in melatonin you start dropping into alpha theta and delta and that\'s when the door opens so what do you wanna drop in there do you wanna do something you wanna drop anything in there that\'s gonna cause you to be more limited or distract you or you know you know cause you to you to think and feel later on the next day a certain way or do you say by volition i\'m gonna teach my body emotionally what my future feels like i\'m gonna keep bringing up this feeling of gratitude because i know that gratitude strengthens my immune system by fifty', 0.8, 0.7, 0.9, 0.6, 0.6, 0.8, 0.6, 'rejected', 'completed', NULL, NULL, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.3, 0.7),
(17, 4, 'Your Evenings Determine Your Days', 'The evening and the morning are two times in the day where the door opens up.', 'This suggests a powerful routine change that can influence overall well-being.', 271624, 322464, 0.6959349593495935, '2026-08-14 12:27:15', 42, 42, 'lesson', 'that\'s the that\'s the joy of change right so so the evening in the morning are two times in the day where your the door opens up you know your brain waves go from beta to alpha to theta to delta in the evening when you wake up in the morning you know you go from delta to theta to alpha to beta so there\'s two times where the door between the conscious mind and the subconscious mind opens and people i mean the people in my my life that that do this they they they they take their time before they go to bed they write things down that are important to them things they wanna change they don\'t wanna watch tv or get on their thing their their their device they really wanna invest in themselves right and they\'re serious about it and as a side effect the of the opportunities the coincidences the synchronicities the serendipities', 0.8, 0.7, 0.7, 0.5, 0.7, 0.8, 0.7, 'selected', 'completed', 266920, 325760, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.4, 0.8),
(18, 5, 'The Darkness of Today\'s World', 'We\'re in a very prophesied time of unrest and uncertainty.', 'This powerful statement creates intrigue about current global issues, making people want to know more.', 0, 47680, 0.8414634146341463, '2026-08-14 13:38:53', 47, 50, 'surprise', 'one of the most challenging things about this time is we\'re in a very prophesied time of unrest uncertainty geopolitical events that are destabilizing climate events that are destabilizing and impactful the rise of darker energies that might want to whether they want it to look like a war or whether they want it to look like people being more divided amongst themselves i think that is the shadow side of what we\'re in as a world and i think for those of us who remember say the nineties or the eighties or the you know even the early or you know the two oh oh ohs i think it\'s quite', 0.9, 0.9, 0.9, 0.7, 0.6, 0.8, 0.9, 'selected', 'completed', 0, 52680, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.8, 0.9),
(19, 5, 'Why Spirituality Isn\'t Always Kindness', 'Being spiritually learned doesn\'t make you more kind.', 'This challenges common assumptions about spirituality and morality, creating an engaging discussion point.', 398000, 401520, 0.8219512195121949, '2026-08-14 13:38:53', 64, 64, 'controversy', 'so you can be a very kind atheist', 0.9, 0.8, 0.9, 0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 0.8, 'selected', 'completed', 395000, 406520, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.9, 0.8),
(20, 5, 'Lessons from an Empath-Narcissist Dynamic', 'You do have to get to a point where you recognize your blind spots.', 'This provides a valuable lesson for personal growth after a toxic relationship, inviting reflection and discussion.', 641760, 703880, 0.7699186991869916, '2026-08-14 13:38:53', 77, 77, 'lesson', 'who we are how we want to interact and what\'s important to us that\'s and that goes back to the empath narcissist dynamic i think think when you come out of one of those relationships you\'re often in grief in horror in shock you can\'t quite believe that someone could have behaved that way and then you know once you get through the more victim aspects of the consciousness and i\'m not making light of that because some people go through horror with narcissists so i\'m not wanting to make light of being a victim to a narcissist in your life but you do have to get to a point where you you recognize ah where were my blind spots how did i walk into that how do i change myself so that i don\'t experience that again because that was the lesson i was being shown that was the learning from this i have to take a learning from this and use it to reclaim myself rather than live in the ashes of feeling annihilated by a relationship or an authority figure', 0.8, 0.8, 0.7, 0.8, 0.7, 0.9, 0.6, 'selected', 'completed', 638760, 708880, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.7, 0.8),
(21, 5, 'Is Spirituality Supposed to Be Easy?', 'I think I thought that spirituality was going to make everything better.', 'This questioning of spirituality\'s role creates an intriguing conversation around expectations and reality.', 482960, 509040, 0.7601626016260161, '2026-08-14 13:38:53', 68, 68, 'surprise', 'and that\'s why we were doing it it\'s like it\'s gonna make everything better and we\'re gonna be enlightened and there\'s gonna be no distress and actually that\'s not earth school there are certainly aspects of spirituality and connection to a faith that can that can root you and that can help you be a better person in the world and help you experience the world in a better way but we\'re here on an evolutionary path and i think too often the construct', 0.8, 0.9, 0.9, 0.5, 0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 'selected', 'completed', 479960, 514040, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.6, 0.8),
(22, 5, 'The Rise of Mystical Experiences', 'More people are having more mystical experiences in the world.', 'This taps into the intriguing trend of spirituality, inviting curiosity about its implications.', 141040, 181640, 0.7422764227642277, '2026-08-14 13:38:53', 53, 53, 'surprise', 'more people are having more mystical experiences in the world with the land people reporting et experiences all of that is very strong right now and that\'s one of the things my guide\'s the z\'s had said they said you\'re gonna go through times on earth that will in a way dismantle your old world and in tandem with that you will see a massive rise in consciousness and at the time they said that maybe fifteen years ago i remember thinking oh i had an idea of what that would look like but what i\'m seeing is it\'s very varied and it\'s very personal recently i was talking to someone who was upset about', 0.8, 0.8, 0.9, 0.5, 0.6, 0.8, 0.8, 'selected', 'completed', 138040, 186640, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.5, 0.8),
(23, 5, 'Faith in Turbulent Times', 'Faith is becoming more important for people in times of turmoil.', 'This observation opens a discussion on faith and spirituality in the face of global crises, making it relatable.', 252000, 293280, 0.7211382113821138, '2026-08-14 13:38:53', 56, 56, 'advice', 'it\'s one of the themes i put in this month\'s energy update there is this weird almost breakdown around what spirituality religion faith is i\'m a big believer in christ consciousness and jesus i can i can connect to that energy and still connect to other energies i don\'t believe i have to be ring fenced into seeing that a certain way so you know that\'s what i was just saying to my friend i said yeah there are those who do that and they point the finger back at where they were and try and destroy it and there are those who go oh i\'ve grown into this and that\'s okay if that\'s how they\'re now experiencing their faith but i think the reason faith is becoming more important for people is in times of turmoil and trouble', 0.8, 0.8, 0.8, 0.6, 0.7, 0.7, 0.6, 'selected', 'completed', 249000, 298280, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.5, 0.7),
(24, 5, 'A Shift in How Faith is Practiced', 'People are walking away from religion during this time or shifting into spirituality.', 'This highlights a significant societal shift that many find relevant and debatable.', 182920, 231240, 0.6934959349593494, '2026-08-14 13:38:53', 54, 54, 'controversy', 'someone that they knew in the spiritual field who was known who had now gone to jesus in christ consciousness and religion which we\'re seeing a lot and vice versa i\'ve also seen people walk away from religion during this time or you know shift into spirituality and the message my guides have always given me is it doesn\'t really matter how you are finding faith for yourself how your faith makes you behave toward others that\'s very interesting so you know i\'ve always said that i personally have never grown up in religion but i support any religion that helps people love each other more and become more of who they\'re here to be and live a more spirit filled life that\'s harmonic i don\'t support religion\'s disguise', 0.7, 0.8, 0.7, 0.4, 0.6, 0.7, 0.7, 'selected', 'completed', 179920, 236240, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.8, 0.7),
(25, 5, 'The Complexity of Spiritual Communities', 'I\'ve seen as much judgment in the spiritual community as there is in any community.', 'This statement brings conflict to light in a typically perceived idyllic space, sparking thought.', 410880, 444920, 0.6853658536585364, '2026-08-14 13:38:53', 66, 66, 'controversy', 'and i think in the same way that in in you know that you can see religious groups fight each other i\'ve seen it in the spiritual field as well you meet people who want to you know feel superior to someone who isn\'t intuitive or they think because they\'ve done thirty ayahuasca trips that they are now far more enlightened than their grandmother who they see as closed minded but actually their grandmother might be the one going around the town checking everyone\'s okay whereas they\'re like off on their own you know their own', 0.7, 0.8, 0.6, 0.5, 0.6, 0.7, 0.6, 'selected', 'completed', 407880, 449920, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.8, 0.7),
(26, 5, 'Dismantling for a Remantling', 'There\'s a dismantling almost for a remantling to happen at this time.', 'This mysterious phrase piques curiosity about personal and collective transformation.', 310760, 322920, 0.6252032520325204, '2026-08-14 13:38:53', 58, 58, 'surprise', 'yeah that uncertainty and that less holding is can totally fill that in the air it\'s but what i\'m hearing and sorry not but and what i\'m hearing is this there\'s a dismantling almost for a remantling', 0.7, 0.7, 0.8, 0.4, 0.5, 0.6, 0.7, 'selected', 'completed', 307760, 327920, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.4, 0.6),
(27, 5, 'The Energy of Cities vs. Small Towns', 'Cities are a good example of seeing how people are doing with all of this.', 'Contrasting the energy of urban versus rural living strikes a relatable chord for many viewers.', 49440, 98120, 0.5869918699186991, '2026-08-14 13:38:53', 51, 51, 'emotion', 'impactful to walk through that as an energy field and i think about the people i meet who in their seventies and eighties who are walking through it and i\'m like wow you have seen some change because the climate is so different and there is this i think very intense energy in the world i felt it when i was touring and i was going to all these different cities you know i would just walk and pay attention and see how people were looking feeling being and of course cities are always a a skewed example because if you go to smaller towns or local more community based places you can feel softer energy but cities are a good example of of seeing how are people doing with all of this and for me there is the the overarching thing i could feel was how exhausting these times are for everyone', 0.7, 0.6, 0.5, 0.6, 0.7, 0.6, 0.5, 'selected', 'completed', 46440, 103120, 'openai', 'gpt-4o-mini', 'hooks-v2', NULL, 0.3, 0.6);
