ithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256&X-Goog-Credential=pyai-control-plane%40aivamodels.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20260814%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request&X-Goog-Date=20260814T122658Z&X-Goog-Expires=604800&X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host&X-Goog-\"}, \"provider\": \"pyai\", \"segments\": [{\"text\": \"you you\'ve said in your research that in your practices and in your work\", \"endMs\": 8160, \"speaker\": \"speaker_1\", \"startMs\": 2880, \"sequence\": 0}, {\"text\": \"that before you b sleep that time is really important and if we practice gratitude ten minutes a day in just about four days of our immunity system get fifty better\", \"endMs\": 20080, \"speaker\": \"speaker_1\", \"startMs\": 9200, \"sequence\": 1}, {\"text\": \"yeah\", \"endMs\": 20320, \"speaker\": \"speaker_2\", \"startMs\": 20080, \"sequence\": 2}, {\"text\": \"is that it yeah so then that is one case and then a lot of people just use instagram for ten minutes by the end of the day right\", \"endMs\": 27680, \"speaker\": \"speaker_1\", \"startMs\": 20480, \"sequence\": 3}, {\"text\": \"what\'s if i grad if i practice gratitude before bed for ten minutes versus i use my instagram for ten minutes what\'s gonna be the difference\", \"endMs\": 38640, \"speaker\": \"speaker_1\", \"startMs\": 28800, \"sequence\": 4}, {\"text\": \"some people can\'t think for themselves because they\'re having something think for them right those images and the stimulation is causing them to really expose their brain to information\", \"endMs\": 50320, \"speaker\": \"speaker_2\", \"startMs\": 38640, \"sequence\": 5}, {\"text\": \"that is causing them to think and feel a certain way what i\'m saying is think and feel on your own right and that\'s the most important thing or think think for yourself so so people who lose the imagination or the skill of dreaming they\'re just relying on something to think for them alright that\'s why nature\'s so great go out and you know spend three days somewhere in nature first day your brain will be all over the place second day it\'ll kinda come down by the third day you\'re like i\'m thinking clearly again because if you don\'t have your device and you\'re looking at the expanse of the sky or mountains or the sea and you\'re opening your awareness your brain gets very organized right so\", \"endMs\": 90600, \"speaker\": \"speaker_2\", \"startMs\": 51600, \"sequence\": 6}, {\"text\": \"a person who\'s understands that when they go to bed at night\", \"endMs\": 95160, \"speaker\": \"speaker_2\", \"startMs\": 91640, \"sequence\": 7}, {\"text\": \"their serotonin levels change to melatonin and when you\'re in serotonin you\'re in beta when you\'re in melatonin you start dropping into alpha theta and delta and that\'s when the door opens so what do you wanna drop in there do you wanna do something you wanna drop anything in there that\'s gonna cause you to be more limited or distract you or you know you know cause you to you to think and feel later on the next day a certain way or do you say by volition i\'m gonna teach my body emotionally what my future feels like i\'m gonna keep bringing up this feeling of gratitude because i know that gratitude strengthens my immune system by fifty\", \"endMs\": 134080, \"speaker\": \"speaker_2\", \"startMs\": 96520, \"sequence\": 8}, {\"text\": \"and if i\'m having a problem with a chronic health condition or you know a immune mediated condition this would be loving to me so i\'m gonna go for ten or fifteen minutes just feeling gratitude or thinking about all the things i\'m grateful for and then i\'m gonna think about all the things that i\'ll be grateful for when they happen i\'m just gonna let myself go just i\'m just gonna play i\'m just let myself go i promise you though person who does that after a period of time is gonna feel very differently than when they spend ten minutes watching instagram right not not not that i have an opinion on it i just know that it\'s it\'s very seductive and and it could it could cause people to become very dependent on it\", \"endMs\": 176160, \"speaker\": \"speaker_2\", \"startMs\": 135120, \"sequence\": 9}, {\"text\": \"that\'s again like if you understand the science between slowing your brain ways down and what you wanna program in there if you\'re serious about a better life you would run through a list of things that were were really important to you and remember to think that way remember to feel that way remember to behave that way the next day or even better how did i do today how was my day when did i react when did i lose my patience when did i get frustrated when did i move out of balance did i blame the person or circumstance was i greater than that okay another day another lifetime another chance my mother used to say new day right another day how am i gonna be if i had the same circumstance in my life right what\'s a better way for for raj to be or joe to be the next day let me remind myself that i could be that way tomorrow i promise you if you\'re sincere just for two two three weeks of doing that you\'ll naturally surprise yourself like wow i really didn\'t react to that person wow i noticed that i was way more calm i noticed that the person that normally pushes my buttons i didn\'t feel that and that\'s one of the crazy things that happens from our community you know they return back into their life under the common things people say is but i return back into my life and people say what happened to you like you what did what what did you do like are you on a new drug are you taking a new medication did you get a face thing what you know what you got a secret you\'re not telling me you look different right because they are different right\", \"endMs\": 267920, \"speaker\": \"speaker_2\", \"startMs\": 177480, \"sequence\": 10}, {\"text\": \"that\'s the that\'s the joy of change right so so the evening in the morning are two times in the day where your the door opens up you know your brain waves go from beta to alpha to theta to delta in the evening when you wake up in the morning you know you go from delta to theta to alpha to beta so there\'s two times where the door between the conscious mind and the subconscious mind opens and people i mean the people in my my life that that do this they they they they take their time before they go to bed they write things down that are important to them things they wanna change they don\'t wanna watch tv or get on their thing their their their device they really wanna invest in themselves right and they\'re serious about it and as a side effect the of the opportunities the coincidences the synchronicities the serendipities\", \"endMs\": 320760, \"speaker\": \"speaker_2\", \"startMs\": 269920, \"sequence\": 11}, {\"text\": \"somehow are coming to them it\'s not like they\'re going and having to get it like somehow it\'s kinda coming to them that\'s all you need that\'s all you need to believe that you\'re the creator of your life right and and why is that important because you\'re gonna wanna do it again you\'re gonna be like and that\'s why our community does the work because they don\'t want the magic to end they don\'t wanna jinx it they\'re like it\'s too good i\'m gonna i\'m not gonna miss my meditation because too many wonderful things are happening in my life that those synchronicities those opportunities opportunities are telling you you are in fact the creator of your life that\'s the that\'s the side effect\", \"endMs\": 360160, \"speaker\": \"speaker_2\", \"startMs\": 322040, \"sequence\": 12}, {\"text\": \"thank you so much eclip enterprise\", \"endMs\": 364400, \"speaker\": \"speaker_1\", \"startMs\": 360160, \"sequence\": 13}, {\"text\": \"eclipse channel subscribe\", \"endMs\": 366720, \"speaker\": \"speaker_1\", \"startMs\": 365680, \"sequence\": 14}], \"durationMs\": 367293, \"speakerCount\": 2, \"providerJobId\": \"job_TjdPz96OPRlLZwztwgoJFbj4\"}', NULL, '2026-08-14 12:26:33', '2026-08-14 12:27:03', '2026-08-14 12:26:06', '2026-08-14 12:27:03', N